# ⚠ THE LINE-ENDING RULE IS LOAD-BEARING ON WINDOWS.
#
# Git on Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites files to CRLF on checkout.
# cloud-init.yaml embeds a bash script, so a CRLF checkout produces a bootstrap that fails
# on the server with errors like:
#     /usr/local/sbin/k3s-starter-bootstrap.sh: line 2: $'\r': command not found
# The box boots, accepts SSH, and is empty — and nothing points at the line endings.
#
# Forcing LF means a Windows contributor gets the same bytes as everyone else, and the
# server gets a script that runs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched by newline normalisation.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
